The web cannot show, set or clear a group's photo (0094, #225): the browser has no file path to hand the core, and the wasm `Core` had no group-photo export. This adds them, and releases the core as 0.43.0 so the web can take them in the lock PR.

## What changes

- `Client::set_group_photo_bytes(conversation, &[u8])` makes the photo from bytes. It checks the conversation is a group and holds the 10 MB source cap, like the path form. Both forms now share one private `send_group_photo`, so the ffi is unchanged.
- `Client::group_photo_bytes(conversation)` returns this device's copy, or `None`.
- The wasm `Core` exports:
  - `setGroupPhoto(conversationId, bytes) -> string`;
  - `clearGroupPhoto(conversationId) -> string`;
  - `groupPhoto(conversationId) -> Uint8Array | null`.

  Errors go through the existing mapping (`not-a-group`, `unsupported-image`).
- `web/src/generated/core.d.ts` is regenerated from the wasm build, as the `web` job's core guard requires.
- The core workspace version is now 0.43.0. `core/artifact.lock.json` moves in the lock PR after the `core-v0.43.0` release.

## Proof

- New test `a_group_photo_from_bytes_is_stored_sealed_and_read_back_as_bytes` (`core/client/tests/sync.rs`). It covers:
  - another member reads back a JPEG;
  - nothing is left after a clear;
  - bytes that are not an image are refused;
  - the object the relay stores is ciphertext: it does not start with the JPEG marker and is not the sender's copy (#225, box 3).

  Asserting instead that the stored object equals the plain copy fails at `sync.rs:3939`.
- A `not-a-group` assertion is added in `core/wasm/tests/error.rs`.
- Checks that pass:
  - `cargo fmt --all --check`;
  - `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`;
  - the two wasm32 clippy runs from `core.yml`;
  - `cargo test --workspace` (331 passed);
  - `pnpm check`.

## Not changed: a server-side 1:1 refusal

The server cannot tell a conversation of two from a group:
- the conversation's `meta` has no kind (`backend/src/modules/messaging/do/conversation-schema.ts:3-8`);
- the roster keeps accounts that have left.

A count there could refuse a real group. The core refuses with `NotAGroup` on every client, and that is the gate.

## Rows
- L07-B pack T2 "heal truth", from the triage of L07-B's open FIX lines. Built: FIX 8372, 8375, 8376, 8356, 8359, 8521, 8522, 8523, 7436, 9448, 8950, 8952, 9315, 8084, 9072, 8537. Partial: 7344 (body digest; effect time open), 8107 (FacadeRowDoor half; the admission worker spawn is open), 8955 (Witnessed path; host-built assessments open). Routed and open: 7379 (Gate), 10811 (producer owners), 8951 (no due-time producer), 9223 (perf only), and 7344's effect time.
- 9315 restricts (ruled with 8712): a non-sole-owner basis files a proposal, never a block.
- Part of the agent-health (OF-568), self-heal and proactivity digest (OF-194) Linear work.

## What now works, and where
- **Agent health** (`dreamer_runner/maintenance/agent_health/**`):
  - silence no longer stands over evidence it cannot read: an attempt with an unreadable capsule of its generation, or an undecodable call receipt newer than its activity, gets no silence card (8372);
  - a blocked-read failure warns and the finding still lands (8375);
  - an open silence card refreshes when its own attempt shows activity again, within the review setting and window (8376);
  - a bad call receipt is skipped and counted, and a trend comparison is Unknown(Withheld) only when the withheld count could turn it (8356);
  - spend counts each scope on its newest member try (8359; the spend code moved, unchanged, to `rollups/spend.rs` first);
  - a Note to a person the caller cannot read answers FORBIDDEN with handle-free text (8537 part b).
- **Code-run activity witness** (L11-B `code_run/activity.rs`, `code_run/dispatcher/host_doors.rs`): host-door work is witnessed (8521); a contended snapshot takes the lock instead of reading as silence, and a poisoned lock warns once and recovers (8522, 8523).
- **Self-heal**:
  - the consent-depth witness is read and built in one snapshot (7436, `self_heal/consent_depth.rs`);
  - an exact code-fix replay rechecks the Grant it was admitted under, and lapses without one (9448, `maintenance/code_fix.rs`, `code_fix/admission.rs`);
  - a manifest rewrite with the same body is no longer read as a new revision (7344, `coach_diagnostic.rs`).
- **Proactivity digest** (`dreamer_runner/maintenance/digest/**`, oneiron-server `ai_host/dreamer/urgent_digest.rs`):
  - an answered harm assessment is remembered in the digest state, so a restart does not re-ask (8950);
  - urgent seen marks are per owner, not vault-wide (8952);
  - an urgent digest names its witness attempt (8955);
  - a policy basis must be the sole owner's own live claims, or it files as a proposal (9315); the door is named file_dreamer_proactivity_policy.
- **Coach host and routes**:
  - the health draft prompt names the frozen observed_brief and the current_task (8084, `ai_host/coach_health.rs`);
  - the sitting distill is sourced from the brief's rows, the sitting and the resolved actors (9072, `ai_host/coach_host.rs` sitting distill, L07-B's range);
  - spawned facade row verbs keep their attempt_ref (8107);
  - an unknown concern card on Note or Steer answers 404, not Refused (8537 part a).

## Outside-lane hunks (named, approved by the Engine 10-26 16:59)
- L11-B: `code_run/dispatcher/host_doors.rs` (one activity_tool line in each of the 6 host-door fns); `code_run/activity.rs` (blocking snapshot with poison recovery, lock() warns once then clears); `code_run/storage/replay_capsule.rs` NEW fn undecodable_step_capsule_in_txn plus one re-export line each in `code_run/storage/mod.rs` and `code_run/mod.rs`.
- L13: oneiron-server `api/call_receipt.rs` (attempt_collector, with_attempt_collector); `api/facade/action_routes/row_door.rs` (the collector field, both row spawns run under it); `api/owner_routes/concern_routes.rs` (move_error maps NOT_FOUND to NotFound("concern_card", card)).

## Tests
Tests are out of scope. Behaviour a test could pin: fewer silence cards with undecodable rows; refreshed silence cards; Unknown(Withheld) comparisons; spend on older retries; urgent results pending for other owners; FORBIDDEN on a Note to an unreadable person; 404 for an unknown card; the digest id hash covers witness.

## Check
Fleet job 1026-180551-8396 (nelly) on head c6fd17c00b after a signed merge of main 3249560440: `## CHECK rc=0` (cargo check --locked --workspace --all-features) and `## CHECK-DEFAULT rc=0` (cargo check --locked -p oneiron-server -p oneiron). merge-tree against main 36fdcfcae3 is clean.

A first-pass Sol review found seven issues:
- fixed here: a refresh writes only onto the card that still names its attempt; withheld bounds count denominators; an asked or trapped attempt still refreshes its card; refreshes respect review-off and the window; the concern route answers 404 only for a missing card;
- deferred to FIX lines: the admission worker spawn (8107) and the host-built assessment witness (8955).

## FIX-LIST
FIX 10934-10942: 7379 to L02 (Gate predicate stamp); 10811 to the producer owners; 7344's effect time (Gate trust time); register's Option; the 8107 FacadeRowDoor-only scope; an undecodable receipt withholds silence broadly; the tests that may pin old behaviour; 8107's admission worker spawn; 8955's host-built assessment witness.

No live deploy: engine-only change.

## Summary

Adds the **indicator guide**: a lay-reader section on indicator pages that explains what the indicator is, how to read it, what peer-reviewed studies say, which public policies have been studied (in Brazil and elsewhere), what it means by income bracket, and purchasing power. The GDP per capita page (`wdi.ny_gdp_pcap_kd`) is the pilot; indicators without a guide render as before.

- **Pipeline**
  - SIDRA classification/category support.
  - 18 new indicators:
    - PNAD Contínua per-capita household income percentiles (table 7438);
    - real medians (7526/7540);
    - WDI PPP, exchange rate, CPI and GDP pc PPP.
  - `brackets.py`: US$250/500/1k/2k per person per month in 2021 PPP dollars, with reais beside them. Population shares are interpolated between percentiles, and study groups are translated into brackets with the conversion shown.
  - `guides.py`: guide model, checks and bilingual rendering with numeric placeholders (ADR 0007).
  - `income_brackets.json` export, plus guide references in `references.bib`.
- **Site**
  - Guide sections, the income-bracket table and charts (series breaks marked), a cross-country price-level table.
  - New "Como ler estudos / Reading studies" page; the references page includes guides.
- **Docs**
  - ADR 0011, the design spec and the implementation plan;
  - CONTRIBUTING (how to write a guide);
  - glossary terms.

## Review

- Each task was reviewed on its own, then the whole branch twice. Findings were fixed in 6c74558 and cef59f0.
- 157 tests pass; ruff is clean; `compilador build` passes; the site builds 92 pages.

